cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use nanotyper, please cite it along with the underlying tools listed in the README."
title: "nanotyper: Nanopore amplicon multilocus sequence typing"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that calls multilocus sequence types (ST) from Oxford
  Nanopore amplicon sequencing of MLST housekeeping genes: medaka consensus per
  locus, BLAST allele assignment against PubMLST, primer-coverage QC with explicit
  PASS/FAIL tiers, and an interactive HTML report. Runs on an ordinary laptop or
  workstation; batch mode processes up to 96 barcodes per run across many runs
  with cross-run aggregation and replicate checks. Version 1.0 ships the
  Escherichia coli Achtman 7-locus scheme; other schemes are added as scheme packs.
authors:
